al-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -18pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.3800000000000001;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Safety and Precautionary Measures: Guidelines for safe handling and working with fiber optics.</span></p></li></ul><p><b style=\"font-weight:normal;\"><br></b></p><h2 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.3800000000000001;margin-top:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:16pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Who Will Benefit from This Course?</span></h2><p></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-inline-start:48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -18pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.3800000000000001;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Telecommunication Engineers: Professionals aiming to enhance their fiber optic skills.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -18pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.3800000000000001;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Fiber Optic Technicians: Those working directly with fiber optics seeking to improve practical skills.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -18pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.3800000000000001;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Beginners in Fiber Optics: Individuals new to the field wanting to build a solid foundation.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -18pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.3800000000000001;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Telecom Engineering Graduates: Recent graduates looking to broaden their expertise and job prospects.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -18pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.3800000000000001;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Technical Trainers and Educators: Instructors updating their knowledge or developing new course material.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -18pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.3800000000000001;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Tech Researchers: Researchers exploring fiber optics innovations and applications across industries.</span></p></li></ul>', '[\"Problem-solving capabilities for common fiber optic issues. \",\"A comprehensive understanding of fiber optic properties and functionality. \",\"Skillful handling of fiber optics including cutting, splicing, and maintenance. \",\"Insights into the practical applications of fiber optics in telecom, industry, and medicine. \",\"Knowledge of fiber optic manufacturing processes and international quality standards. \",\"Heightened safety awareness and the ability to apply protective measures effectively.\"]', '{\" Do I need prior experience to take this fiber optics course? \":\"No prior experience is required. This course is structured for beginners, technicians, and engineers\\u2014starting with basic concepts and moving into practical applications.\"}', 'english', 3, 5, '[]', '[\"Attention to detail \\u2013 Precision is crucial when splicing, connecting, or maintaining fiber optics. Safety awareness \\u2013 Understanding the importance of following safety protocols is essential when working with delicate fiber materials. \",\"Basic technical knowledge \\u2013 Familiarity with general electronics or telecommunications concepts will make learning smoother. \",\"Problem-solving mindset \\u2013 Fiber optics often involves troubleshooting, so logical thinking is key.\",\" Interest in communication technologies \\u2013 A genuine curiosity about how data travels across networks helps you stay motivated. \"]', 119, NULL, 0, 'advanced', '9', NULL, '', 1757970000, 1761219552, 'general', 0, 1, 'upcoming', '', 'the basics and applications of fiber optics', 'Learn the basics and applications of fiber optics with this mini fiber optic course. Register now to become an expert in this vital field!', NULL, 1, 0, 9, NULL, '35212733850ccfcb45253685ec91d71f.jpg', '2025-10-25T14:07');
INSERT INTO `course` (`id`, `title`, `short_description`, `description`, `outcomes`, `faqs`, `language`, `category_id`, `sub_category_id`, `section`, `requirements`, `price`, `discount_flag`, `discounted_price`, `level`, `user_id`, `thumbnail`, `video_url`, `date_added`, `last_modified`, `course_type`, `is_top_course`, `is_admin`, `status`, `course_overview_provider`, `meta_keywords`, `meta_description`, `is_free_course`, `multi_instructor`, `enable_drip_content`, `creator`, `expiry_period`, `upcoming_image_thumbnail`, `publish_date`) VALUES
(29, 'Simulation for Wireless Using ATOLL', '', '<p style=\"text-align: left; line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 24pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" class=\"dropdown-item\"><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Did you know that over 85% of network planning operations in telecom companies rely on advanced simulation tools like ATOLL? The \'Wireless Network Simulation Using ATOLL\' course from My Communication Academy offers a unique transition from theoretical understanding to practical expertise.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.3800000000000001;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:10pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">This course provides deep insights into designing and analyzing 4G and 5G networks using real data simulation projects, signal quality evaluation, and resource management. Participants will explore essential wireless communication topics such as RF basics, OFDM techniques, and professional coverage analysis.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.3800000000000001;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:10pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Whether you\'re new to ATOLL or already familiar with it, you\'ll find a comprehensive curriculum that supports professional advancement. This is the first advanced course of its kind in the Arab world with continuous support and real-world simulation practices.</span></p><h2 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.3800000000000001;margin-top:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:16pt;f