(110, 943, '&lt;p&gt;8. What is the effect of increasing the antenna size on its gain?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"The antenna gain decreases.\",\" The antenna gain increases.\",\" Increasing the antenna size does not affect its gain\",\" Increasing the antenna size causes unpredictable changes in its gain.  \"]', '[\"2\"]', 8),
(111, 943, '&lt;p&gt;9. What is the difference between a standard 1+0 link and a 2+0 multi-link in microwave transport design?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\" The number of channels used\",\" The connection speed\",\"The level of electromagnetic interference\"]', '[\"1\"]', 9),
(112, 943, '&lt;p&gt;10. What is the difference between 1+1 HSB and 2+0 multi-link in microwave transport design?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"The number of channels used\",\"Connection capacity\",\"The level of electromagnetic interference\",\"Availability\"]', '[\"4\"]', 10),
(113, 944, '&lt;p&gt;1. What does a site survey include in a microwave transmission system?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\"   - Evaluating the surrounding environment and potential obstacles.\",\"   - Analyzing user requirements.\",\"   - Determining safety and security.  \"]', '[\"1\"]', 1),
(114, 944, '&lt;p&gt;2. nLOS refers to less than 40% obstruction in the Fresnel zone, affecting communication.&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"1\"]', 2),
(115, 944, '&lt;p&gt;3. Can MIMO technologies be used to overcome obstacles in NLOS conditions?&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"1\"]', 3),
(116, 944, '&lt;p&gt;4- MIMO and XPIC technologies are complementary&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"1\"]', 4),
(117, 944, '&lt;p&gt;5. In which condition is rerouting or MIMO required to overcome obstacles?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\"LOS\",\"nLOS\",\"NLOS\"]', '[\"3\"]', 5),
(118, 944, '&lt;p&gt;6. What is the main goal of achieving QoS (Quality of Service) in a microwave transmission system?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"- Increase transmission speed\",\"Improve voice quality\",\" Provide reliable and stable service\",\"Ensure data security and protection\"]', '[\"3\"]', 6),
(119, 944, '&lt;p&gt;7. What is the main benefit of using Advanced Modulation (AM) technology in a microwave transmission system?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"   - Maintain high-priority service.\",\"   - Improve signal quality.\",\"   - Reduce network delay.\",\"Increase transmission range. \"]', '[\"1\"]', 7),
(120, 944, '&lt;p&gt;8. When increasing spectral diversity, how does it affect the fade margin and multipath?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"Increases fade margin and reduces multipath\",\"Reduces fade margin and increases multipath\",\"Does not affect fade margin or multipath\",\" Increases both fade margin and multipath\"]', '[\"1\"]', 8),
(121, 944, '&lt;p&gt;9. What is the main objective of Path Analysis in a site survey?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\" Identify potential obstacles.\",\"Assess signal strength.\",\"Determine safety and security\",\" Analyze weather conditions\"]', '[\"1\"]', 9),
(122, 944, '&lt;p&gt;10. Is vertical polarization used to reduce the impact of rain on a microwave transmission system?&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"1\"]', 10),
(123, 947, '&lt;p&gt;1.The third generation of optical fibers can transmit data over a distance of 100 km at a speed of 10 Gbps.&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"1\"]', 1),
(124, 947, '&lt;p&gt;2-&amp;nbsp; In FTTH, ONU and OLT are used as the main components.&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"1\"]', 2),
(125, 947, '&lt;p&gt;3- The PON network uses Broadcast technology in the Downlink.&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"1\"]', 3),
(126, 947, '&lt;p&gt;4. What is the necessary condition for total internal reflection, considering the x-axis?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\"  - Reflection occurs when the angle of incidence is greater than the angle of reflection.\",\"  - Reflection occurs when the angle of incidence is greater than the critical angle of refraction.\",\"   - Reflection occurs when the solutions have different refractive indices.           \"]', '[\"2\"]', 4),
(127, 947, '&lt;p&gt;5. What is the definition of partial reflection?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\" - Reflection and refraction of light when transitioning between two mediums.      \",\"   - Complete reflection of light at a large angle.        \",\"  - The angle of incidence is greater than the critical refraction angle.  \"]', '[\"1\"]', 5),
(128, 947, '&lt;p&gt;6.What is the most commonly used frequency band in optical communications?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"C window \",\"L window\",\"S window\",\"K window\"]', '[\"1\"]', 6),
(129, 947, '&lt;p&gt;7. What are the primary materials used in making optical fibers?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\" Optical glass and plastic\",\"Silicon\",\"Aluminum  \"]', '[\"1\"]', 7),
(130, 947, '&lt;p&gt;8. What term refers to the process of thermally fusing the ends of two optical cables to create a continuous and effective connection?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\"Electro-optic fusion welding\",\"Optical fusion splicing\",\"Chemical fusion \"]', '[\"2\"]', 8),
(131, 947, '&lt;p&gt;9. What device is used for splicing optical cables?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"Optical base\",\"Electro-optic fusion\",\" Electro-optic device\",\"Optical fusion splicing device  \"]', '[\"4\"]', 9),
(132, 947, '&lt;p&gt;10. What is the definition of optical refraction?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\"- The bending of light as it passes from one medium to another.  \",\"    - Reflection of light on a rough surface.\",\"Scattering of light in an optical medium.  \"]', '[\"1\"]', 10),
(133, 948, '&lt;p&gt;1. The main benefit of using a Multiplexer in optical fibers is to reduce the cost of optical infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"1\"]', 1),
(134, 948, '&lt;p&gt;2. The primary purpose of using a Circulator in optical fibers is to reduce interference between fibers.&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"2\"]', 2),
(135, 948, '&lt;p&gt;3. The 400nm and 700nm wavelengths are used in optical fibers.&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"2\"]', 3),
(136, 948, '&lt;p&gt;4. The band used in the third window of optical fibers is:&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"o-band\",\"E-band\",\"N-band\",\"L-band &C-band \"]', '[\"4\"]', 4),
(137, 948, '&lt;p&gt;5. The band used for ultra-long waves in the electromagnetic spectrum:&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\"L-band\",\"U-band\",\"c-band\"]', '[\"2\"]', 5),
(138, 948, '&lt;p&gt;6-If we divide the channels in the C-band into parts with a width of 0.8 nm, how many channels will we get using a total of 100G?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"20Ch\",\"40Ch\",\"60Ch\",\"80Ch\"]', '[\"2\"]', 6),
(139, 948, '&lt;p&gt;7. What is the function of a Splitter in Optical fiber?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\"- Combine signals from multiple fibers into one.\",\" - Split power only without the signal.\",\" - Convert optical signals into electrical signals.  \"]', '[\"2\"]', 7),
(140, 948, '&lt;p&gt;8. Uses of a Circulator in optical fibers?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\"   - Direct the flow of signals in optical communication systems.\",\"   - Achieve power balance in optical fibers.\",\"   - Reduce electromagnetic interference in optical fibers.  \"]', '[\"1\"]', 8),
(141, 948, '&lt;p&gt;9. How does an Erbium-Doped Fiber Amplifier (EDFA) work?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\"    - The optical signal is amplified by increasing its strength using an amplified medium containing erbium ions, which interact with the optical signals\",\"    - The optical signal is amplified using materials external to the fibers.\",\" The optical signal is converted into an electrical signal, then amplified and converted back into an optical signal.                                    \"]', '[\"1\"]', 9),
(142, 948, '&lt;p&gt;10. Where is the OTM located in the fiber optic network architecture?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\" - At the end of the network, where it connects to the transmitter or receiver.\",\"  - At network forwarding points, where data is split into multiple channels or combined together.\",\"  - Throughout the network, connecting various network components.\",\"- In optical fiber splitters, where the optical signal is divided into multiple channels.                 \"]', '[\"1\"]', 10),
(143, 949, '&lt;p&gt;1-MS-OTN technology uses the basic structure of OTN for data transmission.&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"1\"]', 1),
(144, 949, '&lt;p&gt;2. Does the Directionless system in CDCG ROADM work by directing optical signals directly without converting them to electrical signals, before adding or dropping optical wavelengths?&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"1\"]', 2),
(145, 949, '&lt;p&gt;3. Are all manufacturers&#039; equipment, such as Huawei or Cisco, installed in the same way?&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"2\"]', 3);
INSERT INTO `question` (`id`, `quiz_id`, `title`, `type`, `number_of_options`, `options`, `correct_answers`, `order`) VALUES
(146, 949, '&lt;p&gt;4. What is the main objective of OTN Hierarchy in optical fibers?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\" - Provide a hierarchical structure for optical data transmission.\",\" - Improve the management and integration of optical networks.\",\" - Increase data transfer capacity and offer multi-protocol services.  \"]', '[\"3\"]', 4),
(147, 949, '&lt;p&gt;5. How is flexibility achieved in Optical Transport Networks using MS-OTN technology?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"   - By increasing the number of optical fibers in the network.\",\"   - Dynamic distribution of data.\",\"   - By improving signal quality in the optical fibers.\",\"   - By enhancing the performance of network devices and equipment.  \"]', '[\"2\"]', 5),
(148, 949, '&lt;p&gt;6. What type of technology is used in ROADM to drop specific wavelengths?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\" (PLC (Planar Lightwave Circuit\",\"(WSS (Wavelength Selective Switch\",\" (OADM (Optical Add\\/Drop Multiplexer\"]', '[\"2\"]', 6),
(149, 949, '&lt;p&gt;7. What does &quot;contentless&quot; mean in CDCG ROADM?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"   - Handling wavelength interference without a negative impact.\",\"  - Avoiding wavelength interference\",\"  - Precisely identifying the necessary wavelengths\",\" Removing specific wavelengths without affecting others\"]', '[\"1\"]', 7),
(150, 949, '&lt;p&gt;8. What are the key factors to consider when designing HLD (High-Level Design)?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"   - System and application functional and non-functional requirements.\",\"      - Required performance, endurance, and stability.  \",\"- Compliance with industry standards and guidelines\",\"all\"]', '[\"4\"]', 8),
(151, 949, '&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;9. Optical transport is considered an inexpensive option&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"2\"]', 9),
(152, 949, '&lt;p&gt;10. What layers are used in MS-OTN technology?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"OTU (Optical Transport Unit) \\u0648 ODU (Optical Data Unit) \\u0648  OCh (Optical Channel).\",\"\\u2022 ( PHY (Physical Layer) \\u0648 MAC (Media Access Control) \\u0648 TCP\\/IP (Transmission Control Protocol\\/Internet Protocol) .\",\"\\u2022 ( PM (Performance Monitoring) \\u0648 FM (Fault Management) \\u0648 CM (Configuration Management).\",\"\\u2022  SDH (Synchronous Digital Hierarchy) \\u0648 SONET (Synchronous Optical Networking) \\u0648 DWDM (Dense Wavelength Division Multiplexing).\"]', '[\"1\"]', 10),
(153, 950, '&lt;p&gt;1- Can microwave technology be considered a suitable option for those seeking to transmit data at high speed?&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"1\"]', 1),
(154, 950, '&lt;p&gt;2-Can more than one operator use the same microwave bandwidth, provided that they operate in different geographical areas?&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"1\"]', 2),
(155, 950, '&lt;p&gt;3-Does the microwave transmission system allow both transmission and reception using the same cable and equipment?&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"1\"]', 3),
(156, 950, '&lt;p&gt;4. Among the following factors, what is the main factor influencing the choice of transmission method?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\" Transmission speed\",\" Implementation cost\",\" Communication reliability\",\" All of the above\"]', '[\"4\"]', 4),
(157, 950, '&lt;p&gt;5. What is the best option for transmitting data at 3.5 GHz over a distance of 400 meters?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\"Coaxial cable\",\" Ethernet network (Wired)\",\"Wireless network\"]', '[\"3\"]', 5),
(158, 950, '&lt;p&gt;6. What is the effect of signal frequency on the performance of an IF (Intermediate Frequency) cable?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"   - Higher frequencies lead to higher attenuation in the cable\",\"- Higher frequencies lead to lower attenuation in the cable.\",\" Higher frequencies increase the signal strength in the cable.\",\"Frequencies do not affect cable performance.\"]', '[\"1\"]', 6),
(159, 950, '&lt;p&gt;7.Do ODU (Outdoor Unit) and IDU (Indoor Unit) need to be from the same manufacturer?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\"   - Yes, they must be from the same manufacturer for optimal compatibility\",\"   - No, ODU and IDU can be from different manufacturers based on requirements.\",\"   - It depends on the type of technology used in the system. \"]', '[\"1\"]', 7),
(160, 950, '&lt;p&gt;8. Where does modulation occur in the microwave transmission system?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\"- In the Outdoor Unit (ODU)\",\"  - In the Indoor Unit (IDU)\",\"- In the antenna.\"]', '[\"2\"]', 8),
(161, 950, '&lt;p&gt;9. When transmitting very large amounts of data in a microwave transmission system, which technology is used?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 2, '[\"PDH\",\"IP\"]', '[\"2\"]', 9),
(162, 950, '&lt;p&gt;10. What frequency band is typically used for wireless backhaul over a distance of 1 km to 10 km in a microwave transmission system?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\"\\u2022 L-band\",\"\\u2022 C-band\",\"\\u2022 E-band\"]', '[\"3\"]', 10),
(163, 951, '&lt;p&gt;1. When determining the height of the transmission tower in a microwave system, the required height depends on whether the distance is near or far, where the height is calculated from the center of the Earth for short distances and from sea level or the center of the Earth for long distances.&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"2\"]', 1),
(164, 951, '&lt;p&gt;2-&amp;nbsp; As distance increases, the Fresnel zone increases and becomes better while keeping other parameters constant.&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"2\"]', 2),
(165, 951, '&lt;p&gt;3-If there is a &quot;drop&quot; in the vertical transmission in a 2+0 no protection design, the connection speed will be affected.&lt;/p&gt;', 'single_choice', 2, '[\"True\",\"False\"]', '[\"1\"]', 3),
(166, 951, '&lt;p&gt;4. Which of the following statements is true?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 4, '[\"   As frequency increases, Fresnel zone obstructions decrease.\",\" As frequency increases, Fresnel zone obstructions increase.\",\" As distance increases, Fresnel zone obstructions decrease\",\" As distance increases, Fresnel zone obstructions increase\"]', '[\"2\"]', 4),
(167, 951, '&lt;p&gt;5. Why is LOS (Line of Sight) necessary in microwave transport systems?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\" To ensure high-quality and efficient signal transmission\",\"To increase interference\",\" To reduce the communication range\"]', '[\"1\"]', 5),
(168, 951, '&lt;p&gt;6. What is the definition of the Fresnel zone?&lt;/p&gt;', 'multiple_choice', 3, '[\"   - An area surrounding the direct path between the transmitter and receiver in a microwave system.\",\"   - An area surrounding the transmitter and receiver in wireless internet.\",\"   - A layer of the atmosphere affecting the propagation of wireless waves.  \"]', '[\"1\"]', 6),
